cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RetainIQ: causal retention decisioning for small subscription businesses"
message: "If you use this software or the SubSim benchmark, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Prasham
    family-names: J
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrashamJ17/PBL-Proj"
abstract: >-
  Churn prediction is a solved commodity; retention decisioning under
  small-sample causal uncertainty is not. This repository contains SubSim, a
  subscription-churn simulator calibrated to published SMB-SaaS benchmarks that
  emits exact ground-truth counterfactuals, and an experiment demonstrating that
  targeting retention offers by churn score destroys value -- performing worse
  than random targeting -- because the customers a churn model ranks highest are
  disproportionately those an intervention harms.
keywords:
  - churn prediction
  - uplift modelling
  - causal inference
  - customer retention
  - treatment effect heterogeneity
  - subscription business
license: Apache-2.0
